{"name":"Amazonian","hex":"#aa6644","fetched":"2026-10-21","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Amazonian","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to the Amazons; aggressive and warlike.","Having to do with the Amazon River in South America, and its surrounding region."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The Amazonian geological period."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Amazonian"}],"entries":[{"title":"Amazonian (Mars)","blocks":[{"text":"The Amazonian is a geologic system and time period on the planet Mars characterized by low rates of meteorite and asteroid impacts and by cold, hyperarid conditions broadly similar to those on Mars today. The transition from the preceding Hesperian period is somewhat poorly defined. The Amazonian is thought to have begun around 3 billion years ago, although error bars on this date are extremely large. The period is sometimes subdivided into the Early, Middle, and Late Amazonian. The Amazonian continues to the present day."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/USGS-Mars-AmazonisPlanitia-mola.jpg/330px-USGS-Mars-AmazonisPlanitia-mola.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazonian_(Mars)","wikidata":"Q391376"},{"title":"Amazon River","blocks":[{"text":"The Amazon River in South America is the largest river in the world by discharge volume of water, and the second-longest or longest river system in the world, a title which is disputed with the Nile."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Amazon_River_ESA387332.jpg/330px-Amazon_River_ESA387332.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_River","wikidata":"Q3783"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/USGS-Mars-AmazonisPlanitia-mola.jpg/500px-USGS-Mars-AmazonisPlanitia-mola.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/USGS-Mars-AmazonisPlanitia-mola.jpg/500px-USGS-Mars-AmazonisPlanitia-mola.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUSGS-Mars-AmazonisPlanitia-mola.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Lava_flow_and_crater_ejecta.JPG/330px-Lava_flow_and_crater_ejecta.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Lava_flow_and_crater_ejecta.JPG/330px-Lava_flow_and_crater_ejecta.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"HiRISE image illustrating superpositioning, a principle that lets geologists determine the relative ages of surface units. The dark-toned lava flow overlies (is younger than) the light-toned, more heavily cratered terrain (older lava flow?) at right. The ejecta of the crater at center overlies both units, indicating that the crater is the youngest feature in the image.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALava_flow_and_crater_ejecta.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Pedestal_crater_and_streaks.jpg/120px-Pedestal_crater_and_streaks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Pedestal_crater_and_streaks.jpg/250px-Pedestal_crater_and_streaks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Pedestal_crater_and_streaks.jpg/120px-Pedestal_crater_and_streaks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APedestal_crater_and_streaks.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thum